WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.136
-The President is already back

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:04.637
to lashing out at his critics

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.372
and taking his cues
from the NRA.

00:00:06.372 --> 00:00:08.408
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:09.842
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.842 --> 00:00:12.945 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:12.945 --> 00:00:14.814
We are now once again

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:17.583
going through the absurd
post tragedy ritual

00:00:17.583 --> 00:00:20.353
of watching the media speculate
over whether Donald Trump

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:22.255
is capable of changing his tone.

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:24.023
The media seems desperate
to believe that Trump

00:00:24.023 --> 00:00:26.692
has a bunch of different tones
and moves and strategies,

00:00:26.692 --> 00:00:27.694
but he doesn't.

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:29.495
He's not a Swiss Army knife.

00:00:29.495 --> 00:00:32.798
He's just a sharp stick.

00:00:32.798 --> 00:00:35.601
Yesterday, he insisted to
reporters that he had already

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:38.838
changed his tone and he began
by stating the obvious.

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:42.875
-What do you say to your critics
that believe that your rhetoric

00:00:42.875 --> 00:00:44.911
is emboldening
white nationalists

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:47.046
and inciting them with anger?

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:49.448
-So, my critics are political
people.

00:00:49.448 --> 00:00:51.183
They are trying to make points.

00:00:51.183 --> 00:00:53.485
-Yes. I agree.

00:00:53.485 --> 00:00:54.953
They are trying to make points.

00:00:54.953 --> 00:00:56.622
That's not a defense.

00:00:56.622 --> 00:00:59.926
That's just a literal
description of what's happening.

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:02.194
[ As Trump ]
So my critics are human beings

00:01:02.194 --> 00:01:05.331
who are forming sentences
with their mouths,

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:07.299
and out of those mouths
are coming words

00:01:07.299 --> 00:01:10.436
that are in English.

00:01:10.436 --> 00:01:11.470
[ Normal voice ]
Sounds like an alien

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:13.205
trying to explain
the rules of basketball.

00:01:13.205 --> 00:01:18.177
"They are tall beings who use
the orange orb to make points."

00:01:18.177 --> 00:01:21.047
Trump can't go a day --
he can't even go a few hours

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:22.248
without fighting with someone

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:23.750
because that's
his favorite thing to do.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.451
It might be the only thing
he likes doing.

00:01:25.451 --> 00:01:28.321
If he weren't President,
he'd be a guy around the city

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:30.323
waiting for someone to
accidentally bump into him.

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:32.158
That's why he always
walks around

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:34.594
with his chest puffed out
like that.

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:36.529
[ As Trump ] Hey [bleep]
Did you bump into me?

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:38.298
You want to go?
Let's go right now.

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:40.433
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:42.535
[ Normal voice ] For example,
just hours after he lied

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:43.903
and said he changed his tone,

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:47.373
Trump found time to respond
to a speech by Joe Biden.

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:51.410
-"Watching Sleepy Joe Biden
making a speech, so boring.

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:53.846
The lame stream media
will die in the ratings

00:01:53.846 --> 00:01:56.148
and clicks with this guy.

00:01:56.148 --> 00:01:58.251
It will be over for them,
not to mention the fact

00:01:58.251 --> 00:02:00.219
that our country will do poorly
with him.

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:03.655
It will be one big crash, but
at least China will be happy."

00:02:03.655 --> 00:02:06.459
-Think about how much
of a narcissist you have to be

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:08.694
to tweet about
how much better you are

00:02:08.694 --> 00:02:10.963
for TV ratings on a day
when you are supposed to be

00:02:10.963 --> 00:02:12.532
consoling victims of a tragedy.

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:15.368
It's like if you crashed
a car while drunk driving

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:16.502
and your first thought was,

00:02:16.502 --> 00:02:18.605
"Oh, my God,
I'm going to be on 'Cops'!"

00:02:18.605 --> 00:02:23.642
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.642 --> 00:02:25.944
Yesterday, Biden was asked
if he wanted to respond

00:02:25.944 --> 00:02:27.313
to any of Trump's attacks
on him.

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:29.081
And he had a very curt response.

00:02:29.081 --> 00:02:32.317
-Do you want to respond to
the president responding to you?

00:02:32.317 --> 00:02:34.186
-He should get a life.

00:02:34.186 --> 00:02:37.757
[ Cheers and applause ]
-That's the problem.

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:40.593
That is the problem right there.

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:44.430
Fighting with people online
is his life.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.632
That's all he wants to do.

00:02:46.632 --> 00:02:50.002
If he were President in 1996
instead of 2019,

00:02:50.002 --> 00:02:52.071
Biden would have gotten
an AOL instant message

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:54.206
from someone named "TheDonald69"
that said,

00:02:54.206 --> 00:02:56.776
"You suck, loser. Sad.

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:58.043
See you at school tomorrow."

00:02:58.043 --> 00:03:01.246
In fact,
Trump seemed to spend all day

00:03:01.246 --> 00:03:02.849
lashing out at people

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:04.750
even if they didn't actually
criticize him.

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:07.419
For example, he picked
a totally bizarre fight

00:03:07.419 --> 00:03:09.355
with the mayor of Dayton,
Nan Whaley,

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:11.323
and Ohio senator Sherrod Brown.

00:03:11.323 --> 00:03:13.492
According to CNN,
after Trump's trip,

00:03:13.492 --> 00:03:15.861
Brown said Trump was received
well by the patients,

00:03:15.861 --> 00:03:17.329
was comforting,
and did the right things.

00:03:17.329 --> 00:03:19.498
Whaley said victims
were grateful to see Trump

00:03:19.498 --> 00:03:22.001
and that he was treated well
by the victims, for sure.

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:23.302
Neither of the two Democrats

00:03:23.302 --> 00:03:26.072
alleged that Trump was badly
received at the hospital.

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:27.339
Now, you might think,
"How could he possibly

00:03:27.339 --> 00:03:28.508
find a way to get mad
about that?"

00:03:28.508 --> 00:03:30.643
Well, if you're thinking that,
congratulations.

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:32.545
You don't have Donald Trump's
brain disease.

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:35.581
Because despite saying
only nice things

00:03:35.581 --> 00:03:37.283
about his reception
at the hospital,

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:38.718
Brown and Whaley
were both subjected

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:40.453
to nasty tweets from Trump.

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:43.356
-The president weighed in,
saying, "Just left Dayton, Ohio,

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:45.124
where I met with the victims
and families,

00:03:45.124 --> 00:03:47.593
law enforcement, medical staff,
and first responders.

00:03:47.593 --> 00:03:49.529
It was a warm
and wonderful visit.

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:51.797
Tremendous enthusiasm
and even love.

00:03:51.797 --> 00:03:53.666
Then I saw
failed presidential candidate,

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:56.335
"Zero Percent" Sherrod Brown
and Mayor Whaley

00:03:56.335 --> 00:03:58.304
totally misrepresenting
what took place

00:03:58.304 --> 00:03:59.705
inside of the hospital.

00:03:59.705 --> 00:04:01.974
-Their news conference after
I left El Paso was a fraud.

00:04:01.974 --> 00:04:03.576
It bore no resemblance
to what took place

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:05.945
with those incredible people
that I was so lucky

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:08.114
to meet and spend time with.
They were all amazing.

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:09.348
-First of all,
in case you missed it,

00:04:09.348 --> 00:04:12.684
he accidentally wrote
"amazing-o."

00:04:12.684 --> 00:04:16.355
Which I guess is a knock-off
version of SpaghettiOs.

00:04:16.355 --> 00:04:18.457
"Dad, we want SpaghettiOs
for dinner!"

00:04:18.457 --> 00:04:19.992
[ As Trump ]
Here, have some Amazing-Os.

00:04:19.992 --> 00:04:22.628
They're just as good.
I bought them at ShopWrong.

00:04:22.628 --> 00:04:24.096
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.096 --> 00:04:25.798
[ Normal voice ] Second,
and I'm asking this sincerely,

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:27.232
what the [bleep]
are you talking about?

00:04:27.232 --> 00:04:29.168
How did you manage to take

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:31.203
what they said about you
and get mad about it?

00:04:31.203 --> 00:04:32.704
What chemical are you missing
from your brain

00:04:32.704 --> 00:04:34.039
that makes you like this?

00:04:34.039 --> 00:04:36.876
Is it the same chemical
responsible for telling you

00:04:36.876 --> 00:04:39.545
which direction to walk in
so you don't amble around

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:41.113
in circles
on the White House lawn

00:04:41.113 --> 00:04:44.884
like an old man who wandered
away from the group home?

00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:46.518
I mean, look at him,
just shuffling around

00:04:46.518 --> 00:04:49.522
like he's looking for
a golf ball.

00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:50.722
[ As Trump ]
You guys seen a Titleist

00:04:50.722 --> 00:04:53.425
with a dollar sign on it?

00:04:53.425 --> 00:04:54.927
[ Normal voice ] Gonna have to
put a sign around his neck

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:57.930
that says, "If found, return
to 1600 Pennsylvania Avenue."

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.365
[ Laughter, cheers,
and applause ]

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:03.602
Then,

00:05:03.602 --> 00:05:05.704
after Trump's
unhinged tweet barrage,

00:05:05.704 --> 00:05:08.608
we got to watch the mayor of
Dayton find out in real time

00:05:08.608 --> 00:05:10.076
that Trump
had tweeted about her,

00:05:10.076 --> 00:05:12.312
read the tweet,
and try to figure out

00:05:12.312 --> 00:05:13.979
what the hell
he was talking about.

00:05:13.979 --> 00:05:15.214
-"Just left Dayton, Ohio.

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:18.217
You got two tweets.<i> Doble.</i>

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:19.886
-"Totally misrepresenting."

00:05:19.886 --> 00:05:24.423
[ Mumbling ]

00:05:24.423 --> 00:05:28.227
-What does the tweet say?

00:05:28.227 --> 00:05:30.096
-I don't -- I mean, like,
I'm really confused.

00:05:30.096 --> 00:05:32.364
We said he was treated, like,
very well, so...

00:05:32.364 --> 00:05:33.733
-I'd love to hear what his --

00:05:33.733 --> 00:05:38.003
-I don't know what he's
talking about misrepresenting.

00:05:38.003 --> 00:05:39.638
Oh, well. You know.

00:05:39.638 --> 00:05:41.674
He lives in his world
of Twitter.

00:05:41.674 --> 00:05:43.843
-You know, it's such a relief
to see a politician

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:46.212
have a normal, human reaction
to Trump's tweets.

00:05:46.212 --> 00:05:48.681
You usually either get
Republicans making excuses

00:05:48.681 --> 00:05:51.283
or Democrats justifiably angrily
denouncing him.

00:05:51.283 --> 00:05:54.020
But it's rare to see someone
in real time just be like,

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:56.455
"What?

00:05:56.455 --> 00:05:59.225
I -- I -- What?

00:05:59.225 --> 00:06:01.226
Well, I mean, I guess somebody

00:06:01.226 --> 00:06:03.029
put something
in his Amazing-Os."

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:04.430
[ Laughter ]

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:06.399
But in that press conference,
Whaley and Brown did offer

00:06:06.399 --> 00:06:07.900
some justified criticisms
of Trump

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:09.569
that had nothing to do with
the hospital visits.

00:06:09.569 --> 00:06:11.370
Brown, for example,
said Trump would never

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:14.673
act on gun violence because
he and Senate Majority Leader

00:06:14.673 --> 00:06:17.543
Mitch McConnell are, of course,
beholden to the NRA.

00:06:17.543 --> 00:06:20.546
-Republicans for years now
have dug in

00:06:20.546 --> 00:06:22.214
and done the bidding of the NRA.

00:06:22.214 --> 00:06:24.750
The National Rifle Association,
the gun lobby

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:27.519
gives millions of dollars
to Republican candidates

00:06:27.519 --> 00:06:31.723
and spends millions and millions
against Democrats like me

00:06:31.723 --> 00:06:34.827
that get an "F" from the NRA,
that stood up to the NRA.

00:06:34.827 --> 00:06:36.662
We can't get anything done
in the Senate

00:06:36.662 --> 00:06:37.930
because Mitch McConnell

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:39.031
and the President
of the United States

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:40.566
are in bed with the gun lobby.

00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:41.867
-That's true,

00:06:41.867 --> 00:06:44.403
but the only quibble I have
is with the metaphor.

00:06:44.403 --> 00:06:46.005
I don't think Trump
ever goes to bed.

00:06:46.005 --> 00:06:47.173
I think he spends all night

00:06:47.173 --> 00:06:49.108
wandering around
the White House lawn

00:06:49.108 --> 00:06:50.876
looking for reporters
to yell at.

00:06:50.876 --> 00:06:53.679
[ As Trump ]
Where are you, Jake Tapper?!

00:06:53.679 --> 00:06:55.514
Come out!
[ Laughter ]

00:06:55.514 --> 00:06:56.982
But it's true, of course.

00:06:56.982 --> 00:06:59.385
Trump takes his marching orders
on gun policy from the NRA.

00:06:59.385 --> 00:07:01.386
In fact yesterday
during a Q&amp;A with reporters

00:07:01.386 --> 00:07:03.989
on the White House lawn
amid a national crisis

00:07:03.989 --> 00:07:05.491
over gun violence
and white supremacy,

00:07:05.491 --> 00:07:07.159
Trump said that
there was no political will

00:07:07.159 --> 00:07:09.395
for a ban on assault weapons
and offered some vague,

00:07:09.395 --> 00:07:11.296
half-hearted comments about
background checks

00:07:11.296 --> 00:07:14.800
where even he seemed unclear on
what exactly he was proposing.

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:18.370
-I have had plenty of talks
over the last two days,

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:20.339
and I think something
is going to be come up with --

00:07:20.339 --> 00:07:21.974
We are going to come up
with something

00:07:21.974 --> 00:07:24.243
that's going to be
really very good,

00:07:24.243 --> 00:07:26.912
beyond anything
that's been done so far.

00:07:26.912 --> 00:07:29.415
I think we can bring up
background checks

00:07:29.415 --> 00:07:30.850
like we have never had before.

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:33.052
I think both Republican
and Democrats

00:07:33.052 --> 00:07:35.554
are getting close to
a bill on --

00:07:35.554 --> 00:07:37.557
to doing something
on background checks.

00:07:37.557 --> 00:07:40.158
-They're doing something
on background checks.

00:07:40.158 --> 00:07:42.227
This is a national emergency,
and he talks about it

00:07:42.227 --> 00:07:44.696
with all the specificity
of a dad who has no idea

00:07:44.696 --> 00:07:45.998
where his kids are.

00:07:45.998 --> 00:07:48.200
"I don't know, I think they're
upstairs doing something

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:51.637
on the computer.
I also think I heard a bobcat."

00:07:51.637 --> 00:07:55.741
But Trump reportedly got a call
from NRA CEO Wayne LaPierre

00:07:55.741 --> 00:07:57.476
warning him to back off.

00:07:57.476 --> 00:07:59.611
-What we are told
by the reporting

00:07:59.611 --> 00:08:01.214
of "The Washington Post"
is that there was

00:08:01.214 --> 00:08:03.782
a Tuesday phone call from
Wayne LaPierre

00:08:03.782 --> 00:08:06.151
with the president
and the message

00:08:06.151 --> 00:08:08.086
from the
National Rifle Association

00:08:08.086 --> 00:08:10.822
would be that
the Trump supporters

00:08:10.822 --> 00:08:15.561
in that powerful organization
would not support the president

00:08:15.561 --> 00:08:19.031
if he were to move forward
with background checks.

00:08:19.031 --> 00:08:21.734
The message from the NRA
to the president was,

00:08:21.734 --> 00:08:23.703
"Careful about doing that."

00:08:23.703 --> 00:08:25.203
That goes against what
the president

00:08:25.203 --> 00:08:26.572
has been saying publicly.

00:08:26.572 --> 00:08:29.041
-Of course it does.
Because you can't trust anything

00:08:29.041 --> 00:08:30.575
this President says publicly.

00:08:30.575 --> 00:08:33.345
First of all, he barely said
anything to begin with.

00:08:33.345 --> 00:08:35.614
I mean, listen
to how vague he was.

00:08:35.614 --> 00:08:37.517
-I think something is going to
be come up with --

00:08:37.517 --> 00:08:39.118
We're going to come up
with something

00:08:39.118 --> 00:08:41.387
that's going to be
really very good,

00:08:41.387 --> 00:08:44.089
beyond anything
that's been done so far.

00:08:44.089 --> 00:08:46.992
-He is a master of using
a bunch of words

00:08:46.992 --> 00:08:48.961
to say absolutely nothing.

00:08:48.961 --> 00:08:50.862
He always sounds like
the guy in a movie

00:08:50.862 --> 00:08:53.399
whose job it is to distract
the security guard

00:08:53.399 --> 00:08:56.035
while his partner steals
a painting from the Louvre.

00:08:56.035 --> 00:08:57.536
[ As Trump ] They are going to
come up with something,

00:08:57.536 --> 00:08:59.605
something that's
gonna be so good, very good,

00:08:59.605 --> 00:09:03.509
beyond anything -- That's right.

00:09:03.509 --> 00:09:06.444
Roll it up.

00:09:06.444 --> 00:09:08.014
[ Normal voice ] Trump
and the NRA are closely linked

00:09:08.014 --> 00:09:09.749
for many reasons,
one of which is something

00:09:09.749 --> 00:09:10.916
they both have in common --

00:09:10.916 --> 00:09:13.118
They are grifters
and scam artists.

00:09:13.118 --> 00:09:15.587
Take for example Trump's visit
to El Paso yesterday.

00:09:15.587 --> 00:09:16.856
This isn't the first time
he's been there.

00:09:16.856 --> 00:09:19.058
In fact, he held a rally there
in February.

00:09:19.058 --> 00:09:22.261
And his campaign racked up more
than half a million dollars

00:09:22.261 --> 00:09:25.464
in expenses owed
to the city of El Paso,

00:09:25.464 --> 00:09:27.766
expenses they still
haven't paid.

00:09:27.766 --> 00:09:29.435
-Donald Trump
is going to El Paso,

00:09:29.435 --> 00:09:32.371
while he still owes the city
of El Paso

00:09:32.371 --> 00:09:37.543
over half a million dollars
from his last visit to El Paso.

00:09:37.543 --> 00:09:39.778
The president has
an outstanding bill

00:09:39.778 --> 00:09:45.551
of $569,204.63

00:09:45.551 --> 00:09:47.786
for police
and public safety services

00:09:47.786 --> 00:09:52.058
associated with a February
campaign rally in El Paso.

00:09:52.058 --> 00:09:53.692
-Man, going back to El Paso

00:09:53.692 --> 00:09:57.296
when you owe the city half a
million dollars is a bold move.

00:09:57.296 --> 00:09:59.865
They're going to have to put
the boot on Air Force One.

00:09:59.865 --> 00:10:02.768
[ Laughter ]

00:10:02.768 --> 00:10:04.303
In fact, the bill...

00:10:04.303 --> 00:10:05.304
[ As Trump ]
Let's get out of here.

00:10:05.304 --> 00:10:08.007
Oh, no!

00:10:08.007 --> 00:10:09.508
[Bleep]

00:10:09.508 --> 00:10:13.345
[ Laughter ]

00:10:13.345 --> 00:10:16.381
[ Normal voice ] In fact, the
bill has actually gotten bigger

00:10:16.381 --> 00:10:17.716
the longer it goes unpaid.

00:10:17.716 --> 00:10:20.385
Trump owed an initial fee
of about $470,000,

00:10:20.385 --> 00:10:24.756
but the city tacked on
a 21% one-time late fee in June.

00:10:24.756 --> 00:10:27.626
And of course Donald Trump
has incurred a late fee.

00:10:27.626 --> 00:10:29.161
That's so him!

00:10:29.161 --> 00:10:31.797
I'm surprised his oval office
desk isn't covered

00:10:31.797 --> 00:10:36.235
in unreturned Blockbuster DVDs.

00:10:36.235 --> 00:10:39.371
[ As Trump ]
You guys seen "Tango &amp; Cash"?

00:10:39.371 --> 00:10:42.040
It's really good.

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:44.176
Lot of chemistry
between the two leads.

00:10:44.176 --> 00:10:46.479
[ Laughter ]

00:10:46.479 --> 00:10:49.982
I'm a Tango guy.

00:10:49.982 --> 00:10:52.151
[ Laughter ]

00:10:52.151 --> 00:10:54.086
Teri -- [ Laughs ]

00:10:54.086 --> 00:10:56.188
[ Laughter ]

00:10:56.188 --> 00:10:58.924
Got a young Teri Hatcher in it.

00:10:58.924 --> 00:11:01.293
[ Laughter ]

00:11:07.532 --> 00:11:09.969
[ Laughter, cheers,
and applause ]

00:11:09.969 --> 00:11:11.570
By the way -- by the way --

00:11:11.570 --> 00:11:13.105
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:13.105 --> 00:11:16.641
By the way, at the same time

00:11:16.641 --> 00:11:19.478
Trump is ignoring a half-million
dollar debt to El Paso,

00:11:19.478 --> 00:11:22.214
he also scheduled a headline
fundraiser in the Hamptons

00:11:22.214 --> 00:11:24.816
where tickets run as high
as $250,000.

00:11:24.816 --> 00:11:26.919
But this is something Trump
has in common with the NRA.

00:11:26.919 --> 00:11:28.787
They're also huge grifters,

00:11:28.787 --> 00:11:30.355
as we learned from
a recent string

00:11:30.355 --> 00:11:32.791
of financial scandals that
have nearly crippled the NRA.

00:11:32.791 --> 00:11:35.494
In fact, just yesterday, "The
Washington Post" reported

00:11:35.494 --> 00:11:38.196
that LaPierre sought to have
the nonprofit organization

00:11:38.196 --> 00:11:39.899
buy him a luxury mansion,

00:11:39.899 --> 00:11:42.101
selecting
a French-country-style estate

00:11:42.101 --> 00:11:44.103
in a gated Dallas-area
golf club,

00:11:44.103 --> 00:11:46.105
a 10,000-square-foot estate

00:11:46.105 --> 00:11:47.940
with lakefront
and golf course views

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:50.008
on the market
for about $6 million.

00:11:50.008 --> 00:11:52.511
A $6 million mansion in Texas.

00:11:52.511 --> 00:11:54.546
Meanwhile, in New York,
$6 million will get you

00:11:54.546 --> 00:11:57.949
a two-bedroom condo, and your
landlord is an actual rat.

00:11:57.949 --> 00:12:00.418
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:12:00.418 --> 00:12:04.723
This explains so much, so much
about politics right now.

00:12:04.723 --> 00:12:07.392
Donald Trump and his fellow
grifters on the right

00:12:07.392 --> 00:12:10.161
sell their base racism
and paranoia, and all the while,

00:12:10.161 --> 00:12:12.364
they and their wealthy patrons
are cashing in.

00:12:12.364 --> 00:12:15.400
We have seen corruption and
racism from presidents before.

00:12:15.400 --> 00:12:17.102
But what Trump is doing now
is...

00:12:17.102 --> 00:12:20.205
-Beyond anything
that's been done so far.

00:12:20.205 --> 00:12:22.174
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:22.174 --> 00:12:23.675
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:23.675 --> 00:12:26.245 line:0%
♪♪

